{
  "notes": [
    "This is a provenance scenario for check-threat-model.py (D12) and the Phase 2 half of the run-level record. run/ is the {out} directory: threats.md, the architecture snapshot, and tachi-build/ (named .tachi-build/ in a working directory, which .gitignore excludes here). Every absolute path in a record and a brief names the root /synthetic-case, which materialize() replaces with a real directory. The files hold exactly what the contracts' key sets allow, and test_fixture_374.py reads each one back through the shipped validators.",
    "The planned set follows from phase1/dispatch.json and the roster alone: 14 dispatches, one for each agent with a component in scope, in the roster's order (dsp-001 to dsp-014). A planned record's scope is that agent's components, in the inventory's order.",
    "Every finding's provenance is in provenance.findings: class 1 (a dispatch record keeps it), 2 (a baseline carry-forward) or 3 (Phase 3.6's rule). A record's local IDs are its agent's own: its emitted prefix and a number from 1 in its report's order, so they can equal another finding's final ID. The ID map holds one disposition for each local ID, in order. These values are worked out here from the contracts and are not read from any script: no check script exists yet, and T095 and T096 are the first to run one on them.",
    "run/ holds no run-level plan, no hand-off and no sections.json: tachi-stage.py plan --stage threat-model writes the plan, the check writes its hand-off under that plan's checks/ directory, and a test that needs the manifest or the threats-md parts builds them itself. Section 6 and the other tables of threats.md are the generator's (render_threats_md), as in every other scenario.",
    "The run has no baseline, so every finding is NEW and every brief's baseline_focus is null (a stateless run). threats.md has no Section 4c or 8 and its front matter has no baseline.",
    "Two lineages. A planned dispatch is split into one replacement for each component of its scope, and a replacement that ends early is repeated once: dsp-007 (tachi-agent-autonomy's planned dispatch) ended after 2 findings, with reason no_end_marker, and is split into dsp-015 to dsp-018; dsp-009 (tachi-human-trust-exploitation's planned dispatch) ended with no report, with reason agent_failed, and is split into dsp-019 to dsp-022; dsp-016 (tachi-agent-autonomy's replacement for planner-agent) ended with no report, with reason timed_out, and is repeated by dsp-023; dsp-021 (tachi-human-trust-exploitation's replacement for worker-2) ended after 1 finding, with reason overflow_error, and is repeated by dsp-024. A superseded record's findings are not in the ID map, and no other record names them.",
    "Phase 2's counts: 14 planned, 10 retried (a split of k components counts k, a repeat one), 24 dispatched, 20 done, 4 split and 0 exhausted."
  ],
